MacPaw today launched its <a href="https://moonlock.com">Moonlock</a> cybersecurity app for the iPhone, bringing the company's consumer-focused security features to mobile for the first time.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/Moonlock-macpaw.jpg" alt="" width="1034" height="582" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1077892" /><br/>
Moonlock is designed to help iPhone users recognize and avoid phishing scams and other online threats, according to the company. For example, one of its key features is Scam Detect, which can check suspicious messages and their contents – like screenshots, links, and QR codes – for signs of phishing. <br/>
<br/>
Users just paste, scan, or share the content directly with Scam Detect, and the Moonlock app will analyze it and provide an assessment explaining why it may be suspicious.<br/>
<br/>
Moonlock includes a number of other security features specific to the iPhone. Safe SMS is an opt-in feature that automatically filters out scam texts, with a record of what was caught and why. Meanwhile, Security Score provides a score from 0 to 100 that reflects the iPhone's security setup, and gives users recommendations on how they can improve it.<br/>
<br/>
With Email Breach History, users can check whether their email address has turned up in a data breach. If so, the feature can reveal the source of the breach, when and what was exposed, and then walk the user through the steps required to secure each affected account.<br/>
<br/>
Moonlock also includes a number of device and network checks, and the app aims to help users review things like their Wi-Fi security, passcode protection, iOS updates, and more, with checklists of recommended one-time actions and step-by-step instructions.<br/>
<br/>
